-- title:
--   Deformation package from a distinguished j-expansion
-- statement:
--   Let $q\neq 2$ be a prime, $k$ a field of characteristic $q$ and $E_0$ an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$. Let $W_0$ be a complete discrete valuation domain (complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal) whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$, equipped with a surjective ring homomorphism $\mathrm{res}_0:W_0\to k$ whose kernel is that maximal ideal. Let $\mathcal E$ be a Weierstrass curve over $W_0[[t]]$ with $\Delta_{\mathcal E}$ a unit, whose base change along $\mathrm{res}_0\circ(\text{constant coefficient})$ equals $E_0$, and such that the Hasse invariant of $\mathcal E$ reduced mod the maximal ideal — the coefficient of degree $q-1$ in the $((q-1)/2)$-th power of the two-torsion polynomial of $\mathcal E\otimes k[[t]]$, an element of $k[[t]]$ — has vanishing constant term and nonzero $t$-coefficient. Assume further that for some $a_0\in W_0$, some $e\ge 1$, some unit $u_2\in W_0[[t]]$ and some monic $P\in W_0[X]$ of degree $e$ with $P_i\in\mathfrak m_{W_0}^{\lfloor (e-i)q/(q+1)\rfloor+1}$ for all $i<e$, one has $j(\mathcal E)-a_0=u_2\cdot P(t)$, where $j(\mathcal E)$ denotes `jOfUnit`, the $j$-invariant formed using the unit $\Delta_{\mathcal E}$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a Weierstrass curve $\mathcal E'$ over $W_0[[t]]$ with unit discriminant, again base-changing to $E_0$ along $\mathrm{res}_0\circ(\text{constant coefficient})$, together with a commutative formal group $F^u$ over $W_0[[t]]$ whose underlying two-variable series is $\mathcal E'.\mathtt{formalGroupLawFixed}$ and which satisfies $F^u.\mathtt{IsBaseChange}$ along $\mathrm{res}_0\circ(\text{constant coefficient})$ with $E_0.\mathtt{formalGroup}$, i.e. the series of $E_0.\mathtt{formalGroup}$ is the coefficientwise image of that of $F^u$; writing $\gamma\in W_0[[t]]$ for the coefficient of $Z^q$ in $F^u.\mathtt{nthSeries}\ q$ (the $q$-fold iterate of the group law, $[q]$), the $t$-coefficient of $\gamma$ is congruent to $1$ modulo $\mathfrak m_{W_0}$ and $\gamma-u_1 t$ lies in the ideal generated by $q$ for some unit $u_1\in W_0[[t]]$; and there are $a_0'\in W_0$, $e'\ge 1$, a unit $u_2'\in W_0[[t]]$ and a monic $P'\in W_0[X]$ of degree $e'$ with $P'_i\in\mathfrak m_{W_0}^{\lfloor (e'-i)q/(q+1)\rfloor+1}$ for $i<e'$ such that $j(\mathcal E')-a_0'=u_2'\cdot P'(t)$.
--
--   This is the step that upgrades an explicit Weierstrass family over $W_0[[t]]$, whose mod-$q$ Hasse invariant has a simple zero at $t=0$ and whose $j$-invariant admits a distinguished-polynomial expansion, to the full package of data (reduction to $E_0$, commutative formal group lifting $\widehat{E_0}$, normalised $Z^q$-coefficient of $[q]$, and distinguished expansion of $j$) required downstream. It is used in the construction of the explicit family for $q=3$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_exists_powerSeries_lift_coeff_nthSeries_sub_mul_X_mem_span_and_jOfUnit_sub_eq_mul_eval_of_coeff_hasseInvariant_map.lean

